        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>RetrievalCallback</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::rag::knowledge_gap::RetrievalCallback</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Callback type for dynamic document retrieval in the FLARE loop. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The callable receives a reformulated query string and the maximum number of documents to return (k). It must return a (possibly empty) vector of <ref refid="structthemis_1_1rag_1_1knowledge__gap_1_1_retrieved_document" kindref="compound">RetrievedDocument</ref> values. An empty return value is interpreted as &quot;no
additional documents found&quot; and stops the FLARE iteration early.</para>
<para>Example wiring with VectorIndexManager: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">detector-&gt;setRetrievalCallback(</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>[&amp;vec_mgr,<sp/>&amp;db](</highlight><highlight class="keyword">const</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>std::string&amp;<sp/>q,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">size_t</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>k)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>-&gt;<sp/>std::vector&lt;RetrievedDocument&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>embedding<sp/>=<sp/>embed(q);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(embedding.empty())<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>{};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>[st,<sp/>results]<sp/>=<sp/>vec_mgr.searchKnn(embedding,<sp/>k);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(!st.ok)<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>{};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/><ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1rag_1a8c55ddf4bc0edaaa3205132555fc033c" kindref="member">rag::convertToRetrievedDocuments</ref>(results,<sp/>db);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Retrieval callback invoked by FLARE active retrieval.</para>
<para>F5-2: The callback receives the query, max result count, and a tenant identifier. The tenant_id MUST be forwarded to the underlying vector store so that dynamic re-retrieval always queries the same tenant&apos;s document corpus as the original request — without this, a reformulated FLARE query can silently cross tenant boundaries. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
