      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="namespacethemis_1_1rag_1_1knowledge__gap_1ad6aad72fb6fd4554e85a84020a3f3b64" prot="public" static="no">
        <type>std::function&lt; std::vector&lt; std::string &gt;(const std::string &amp;<ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1query" kindref="compound">query</ref>, size_t num_samples)&gt;</type>
        <definition>using themis::rag::knowledge_gap::LlmSampleFn = 
std::function&lt;std::vector&lt;std::string&gt;(const std::string&amp; query,
                                       size_t             num_samples)&gt;</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>LlmSampleFn</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::rag::knowledge_gap::LlmSampleFn</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Callback type for LLM-based self-consistency sample generation. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>When injected via <ref refid="classthemis_1_1rag_1_1knowledge__gap_1_1_knowledge_gap_detector_1a5d59ae754d21b368a79dac079b21b632" kindref="member">KnowledgeGapDetector::setLlmSampleFn()</ref>, the <computeroutput>generateMultipleSamples()</computeroutput> internal method delegates to this function instead of the built-in heuristic sentence-cycling path.</para>
<para>The callable receives:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>query</computeroutput> The original user query.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>num_samples</computeroutput> The requested number of answer candidates.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>It must return a vector of strings (answer candidates) of any non-zero size. An empty return value causes <computeroutput>generateMultipleSamples()</computeroutput> to fall back to the heuristic path.</para>
<para>Example wiring with an ILLMPlugin: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">detector-&gt;setLlmSampleFn(</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>[&amp;<ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1llm" kindref="compound">llm</ref>](</highlight><highlight class="keyword">const</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>std::string&amp;<sp/>q,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">size_t</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>n)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>std::vector&lt;std::string&gt;<sp/>samples;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>samples.reserve(n);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">for</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">size_t</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>i<sp/>=<sp/>0;<sp/>i<sp/>&lt;<sp/>n;<sp/>++i)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>samples.push_back(<ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1llm" kindref="compound">llm</ref>.generate(q,<sp/>0.8f));<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>temperature</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>samples;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
